`filter()` lang — ibabalik niya 'yung mga items na pumasa sa condition:

```js
const nums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6];
const evens = nums.filter(n => n % 2 === 0);
console.log(evens); // [2, 4, 6]
```

oo naman!

```js
const mga = [{ pangalan: "Ana", edad: 17 }, { pangalan: "Ben", edad: 20 }];
const adult = mga.filter(p => p.edad >= 18);
```

'yung `p` = bawat object sa array

ez lang 'to 😄 sa parent: `display: flex;` tapos `justify-content: center;` (horizontal) at `align-items: center;` (vertical):

```css
.container {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  height: 100vh;
}
```

tip: kung iisang item lang, `margin: auto` sa child minsan mas simple. kung marami, flexbox pa rin 'yung pinaka-reliable. wag kalimutan 'yung `min-height` kung full-screen centering 'yung habol HAHA

add mo lang `flex-direction: column;` sa container:

```css
.container {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
}
```

ngayon vertical na 'yung stack.

debug mode 🐞 ilagay mo 'yung `console.log()` sa mga suspek mong lines:

```js
function add(a, b) {
  console.log("a:", a, "b:", b);
  return a + b;
}
```

makikita mo 'yung values sa browser console (F12 → Console).

async/await sa JS — para 'yung async code mo, readable na parang sync 😄 halimbawa:

```js
async function getData() {
  const res = await fetch("https://api.example.com/data");
  const data = await res.json();
  console.log(data);
}
getData();
```

meaning: hihintayin ni `await` 'yung result bago mag-next line

kung magka-error? `try/catch` na:

```js
async function getData() {
  try {
    const res = await fetch(url);
    const data = await res.json();
    console.log(data);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error("May error:", err);
  }
}
```

oo, mas readable nga 'yon:

```js
async function getData() {
  const res = await fetch("https://api.example.com/data");
  const data = await res.json();
  console.log(data);
}
```

call mo lang `getData()`

lagay ka lang ng `display: grid` sa container:

```css
.container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr 1fr;
  gap: 1rem;
}
```

tatlong column na may iba't ibang lapad 'yan. pwede mo ring i-play around 'yung `justify-items` at `align-items` para ma-center 'yung content sa cells

pwede ring `grid-template-areas`:

```css
.layout {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-areas:
    "header header"
    "sidebar main";
  grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
}
.header { grid-area: header; }
.sidebar { grid-area: sidebar; }
.main { grid-area: main; }
```

mas readable 'to kesa sa puro line numbers

at kung mobile, mag-isa lang 'yung column gamit ang media query

`useState` = hook para mag-store ng state sa function component:

```jsx
import { useState } from "react";

function Counter() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);
  return (
    <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>
      Clicked {count} times
    </button>
  );
}
```

`count` 'yung value, `setCount` 'yung nag-uupdate. pwede ka rin mag-multiple useState sa isang component — hiwalay na state per variable, mas malinis:

```jsx
const [name, setName] = useState("");
const [age, setAge] = useState(0);
```
